11. Modern Tooling & Docker Compose Invariant: When user stories specify test harnesses, black-box validation suites, containerized services, or Makefiles, the DoD MUST explicitly pin 'docker compose -f docker-compose.e2e.yml up --build --exit-code-from ...' (Docker CLI v2 subcommand with a space). The legacy standalone 'docker-compose' (hyphenated binary) is strictly forbidden across all user stories, Makefiles, and test harnesses.
12. Thin Shell Entrypoint Pattern: Mandate that primary executable entrypoints (`main.rs`, `main.go`, `main.py`, `server.ts`, `Main.java`) are thin wrappers (< 15 lines) that immediately delegate to a testable core entrypoint function (`run(args, io) -> Result`, `create_app()`, `WorkerEngine`), enabling fast in-process testing of the complete application lifecycle without spawning external OS processes during intermediate component tasks.
13. Mandatory Makefile Targets (Build, Test, E2E): When a project specifies or generates a Makefile, the Definition of Done MUST mandate three standard recipes: `build` (compiles the binary), `test` (compiles and runs unit tests, strictly exiting with code 1 if 0 tests are found), and `e2e` (physically executes real black-box E2E test scenarios against the running application covering at least one specific scenario for EACH feature, command, and flag declared in SPEC.md, asserting real domain responses and exit code 0; never author empty or tautological e2e recipes). Every Makefile MUST include an `e2e` recipe with per-feature test scenarios.
14. Negative Specification Constraints & Forbidden Tools Mandate: Carefully inspect SPEC.md for any negative constraints, forbidden frameworks, disallowed libraries, or prohibited tools (e.g. 'pytest is strictly forbidden', 'no external web frameworks', 'use only standard library unittest'). The Definition of Done and Acceptance Criteria in EVERY user story MUST explicitly declare these prohibitions and mandate the approved alternative, so downstream generators, planners, and testers never import, configure, or invoke forbidden tools.

